\cf0 Introducing the "0731" Tennis Racket Holder.\
This piece was born from a challenge: My good friend wanted a custom rack for his 30th birthday, but living in different states meant I couldn't ship a bulky, fully assembled unit. I needed a design that used zero glue and zero fasteners-just pure joinery.\
Inspired by the iconic cable-stayed bridges of our hometown, I utilized traditional mortise and tenon joints held together by tension. The slats are wedged so securely that the internal pressure makes them nearly impossible to pull out by hand. I finished it off with custom brass pins to secure the crossbar.\
It's 9 months late for the big 3-0, but it's finally home. Named after our city's area code, this piece is a nod to our roots and a celebration of a lifelong friendship.\
\
==========================================================================================================\
Introducing "SMS" whiskey cabinet\
This piece is the physical epitome of my research and a gift of gratitude for my advisor. Its geometric form is inspired by the solution path of our novel method, the Shifted Maximum Subarray (SMS) algorithm. Moving far beyond mere utility, this cabinet holds deep sentimental value for both of us. I hope he gets to enjoy many well-deserved drinks poured from it for years to come.\
\
