Introducing the "mushroom" side table\
This is the last project of the summer and concludes my makerspace journey at NovaLabs. As you might notice, I've made a series of end tables this summer, trying different designing ideas and joining techniques.\
The design is inspired by mushrooms and is one of my favorite foods, hence the name. This is a prototype and I'll keep working on the joinery for the leg and the top, currently it's connected by a plywood platform because I was rushing towards the end. I also need to make it more balanced so perhaps a tapered leg on the bottom, the second slide shows that the side view is a little "flimsy". This could also be a great opportunity to get into power carving. Endless possibilities.\
Made from oak with a hint of walnut.\
\
