\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Introducing the \'93Kachina tree\'94 end table\
This piece is heavily inspired by the kachina tree cave in Sedona, AZ (see last slide). I was on a mission to explore all the caves in Sedona one time and stumbled upon the lesser known Kachina Tree Cave. At the end of the trail, at a certain angle, you\'92re able to capture the tree-in-a-cave view.\
I wanted to build this end table surrounding that idea that whoever owns this piece can find beauty and peace through the table legs, finding new perspectives of their homes at some special angle.\
The table top has complementary curves to the legs, just like how the tree and the cave complete each other.\
Made with oak, finished with India ink and hard wax oil.\
