\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Introducing the \'93Serenity\'94 Coffee Table\
This is a commission from my landlord. After showing him my previous work, he got really interested in hiring me for a build. He picked out the style and table legs and I made it happen.\
I got a taste of what dealing with a client is like. You don\'92t have much freedom in design, and need to educate them on different species of woods, profiles, and finishes. It\'92s a learning process for both sides, and it\'92s interesting that this was never a problem to me before because I was building stuff for myself. For example, I presented a design to mimic the old coffee table he had in the living room with a lot of details added in the joints (mortise and tenon, through tenon with wedges, etc), but declined by the client because \'93it looks the same as the old table\'94. Mind you the old table was made of MDF with veneer and painted blue, joined by butt join or nails. I\'92m happy that it worked out in the end, but this is a lesson to learn for running a woodworking business, or any business.\
Solid 8/4 walnut, finished with hard wax oil. Measured 48\'94 x 20\'94\
